  "limitations": [
    "The gate covers two neutral-input, NTSC Debug-ROM B01 attempts from startup through the natural tick-720 timeout breakpoint. It observes ordinary renderer commits through renderer tick 719.",
    "The gate reads cumulative renderer/DMA/VBlank counters, bounded capacity telemetry, the complete 68000 audio-status shadow, and the Z80 hardware V-int clock. It is not a CPU-cycle profiler and does not quantify remaining VBlank or simulation headroom.",
    "The cross-clock guard permits at most 32 more Z80 hardware V-ints than delivered 68000 VBlank handlers at the terminal stop. This conservative startup allowance covers the observed 25-V-int pre-display/startup phase with seven V-ints of margin; it does not waive drift accumulated during gameplay.",
    "The gate does not cover PAL double-step frames, reset/completion DMA, Program Stable, other encounters, visual correctness, physical hardware, or Release-ROM equivalence.",
    "A pass cannot waive a nonzero counter from any other genuinely uninterrupted run of the same hashes; such a result is a real fault until explained and fixed."
